  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656086",
      "title": "More on View Encapsulation",
      "lectureOrder": 396,
      "videoOrder": 366,
      "sourceHash": "c1f0917bae9146ec1b4a45538624f1760136fb07728680f44d2408cd13f28bdc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.85,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "you learned how angular encapsulates your styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 10.53,
          "en": "Now you can override this encapsulation though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.53,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "If you go back to your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "to the server element component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 18.18,
          "en": "you can add something to the ad component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.18,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "It's called encapsulation this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "And there as a value you can access a view encapsulation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "which needs to be imported from at angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "So make sure to add this import and then you can choose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "between free modes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 35.31,
          "en": "emulate it as the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.31,
          "end": 37.59,
          "en": "So you don't need to add this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.59,
          "end": 38.423,
          "en": "None,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.423,
          "end": 40.32,
          "en": "If you add this, would makes sure that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.32,
          "end": 42.4,
          "en": "if we have a look at our component again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.38,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "and we inspect our server element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 51.77,
          "en": "that now in here we don't see these strange attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.05,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "being added to our elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "Therefore this component now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "does not use view encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.8,
          "en": "The other components still will use it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.8,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "You still see these attributes but if you now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "define any styles for this component in these CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 72.06,
          "en": "of this component they will actually get up light globally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 76.11,
          "en": "And I can demonstrate this by going into this CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.11,
          "end": 78.84,
          "en": "And if I change the label color and the label is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.84,
          "end": 81.723,
          "en": "in the cockpit not in this component to red,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "yeah now you will see the label there is overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "Whilst this label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "of course still has its custom unique attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "it still is a label in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 95.03999999999999,
          "en": "And in this server element component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.03999999999999,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "we disable encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "So there our selectors aren't changed by angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "They don't receive their unique selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 107.03999999999999,
          "en": "therefore they are enforced they are used application wide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.03999999999999,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "also affecting other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 111.69,
          "en": "Might be the behavior you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "chances are that this is not the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "but it's important to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "that you can change this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "Now besides None you also could choose native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 126.09,
          "en": "and native uses the ShadowDom technology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.09,
          "end": 128.67,
          "en": "This should give you the same result as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "with emulated but only in browsers which supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "Which is why for most cases you want to choose emulated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "but be aware that you could switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "to None or Native year two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "So I will go back to emulated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 143.88,
          "en": "which again you wouldn't have to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "It's a default anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "With that our label should no longer be red now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 150.12,
          "en": "So that is how you can change it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.12,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "and how view encapsulation works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 155.4,
          "en": "A nice tool ensuring that by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.4,
          "end": 159,
          "en": "only your component receives the styles you define for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 159,
          "end": 161.223,
          "en": "But as you learned it can be overwritten.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
